# Rank 1359 / CVE-2023-36460 (GHSA-9928-3cp5-93fm): Mastodon's Attachmentable
# concern wrapped Paperclip's `has_attached_file` and forced
# `validate_media_type: false` onto every attachment in the application, which
# is the option that removes Paperclip's MediaTypeSpoofDetectionValidator from
# the record's validation chain. The substitute ran instead inside
# `before_<name>_post_process`:
#
#   options = { validate_media_type: false }.merge(options)
#   super(name, options)
#   send(:"before_#{name}_post_process") do
#     ...
#     Paperclip::Validators::MediaTypeSpoofDetectionValidator.new(attributes: [name]).validate(self)
#   end
#
# An ActiveModel validator's `validate(record)` only appends to `record.errors`;
# it returns no verdict and halts nothing. Invoked from a post-processing
# callback, its errors are never consulted, so a file whose real type disagreed
# with its claimed one hands to the ImageMagick and ffmpeg post-processors
# anyway. Crafted media then drove those processors into writing and deleting
# files outside the attachment directory -- arbitrary file creation, and from
# there remote code execution (CWE-434).
#
# Fix dc8f1fbd97, the merge of the advisory's private branch, drops the
# `validate_media_type: false` default so Paperclip validates the media type
# itself, and moves the remaining callbacks to `before_<name>_validate` so they
# run before anything is processed. It also raises instead of returning the
# original file from lib/paperclip/transcoder.rb and ships an ImageMagick
# policy. The pool row's commit is that merge: it carries the four advisory
# fixes and no release bump, and the advisory records 4.1.3/4.0.5/3.5.9 as the
# releases it went out in.
#
# FIXED. The vulnerability is a security control switched off by configuration,
# so nothing is tainted and nothing resolves -- baseline reports only
# VYQL-RES-001 resource-handle findings on the same trees. The Ruby class
# context carries the option as the structured fact
# `field:validate_media_type=false`, so a binding is all that is missing;
# code.UncheckedUploadedImageProcessing and rule VYQL-INJ-043 (CWE-434)
# judge an uploaded image reaching a processor unchecked, and are reused rather
# than minted.
#
# The option name is what keeps this off ordinary code: `validate_media_type` is
# Paperclip's own switch for spoof detection and means nothing elsewhere, and
# the binding requires it set to false by exact token match rather than by
# substring, so an attachment that leaves the validator in place is not
# reported. Class scope, not module scope, keeps the fact inside the declaring
# class's own body.
#
# Measured bounded (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off) over
# app/models/concerns, app/models/media_attachment.rb and lib/paperclip: at
# dc8f1fbd97^ 4 findings before the binding and 5 after, the extra one being
# VYQL-INJ-043 at attachmentable.rb:5; at dc8f1fbd97 3 findings with no
# VYQL-INJ-043. Whole-tree mastodon at dc8f1fbd97^ reports 390 findings, four of
# them VYQL-INJ-043, and every one is a real `validate_media_type: false` --
# attachmentable.rb plus custom_emoji.rb, preview_card.rb and
# preview_card_provider.rb, which pass the option directly and which the fixed revision
# leaves alone because those attachments are fetched by the server rather than
# uploaded. No other site in the tree is reported. loofah, rack, sanitize and
# mail report no VYQL-INJ-043, and the spec suite is unchanged at 4757 passing
# specs.

test "rank1359: an attachment declaration that disables Paperclip's media-type validation and re-runs the spoof detector after processing has begun"
  lang ruby
  file app/models/concerns/attachmentable.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-043
  code
  ```
  module Attachmentable
    extend ActiveSupport::Concern

    included do
      def self.has_attached_file(name, options = {})
        options = { validate_media_type: false }.merge(options)
        super(name, options)
        send(:"before_#{name}_post_process") do
          attachment = send(name)
          check_image_dimension(attachment)
          set_file_content_type(attachment)
          obfuscate_file_name(attachment)
          set_file_extension(attachment)
          Paperclip::Validators::MediaTypeSpoofDetectionValidator.new(attributes: [name]).validate(self)
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1359: the fixed revision leaves Paperclip's media-type validation on and moves the callbacks ahead of processing"
  lang ruby
  file app/models/concerns/attachmentable.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-043
  code
  ```
  module Attachmentable
    extend ActiveSupport::Concern

    included do
      def self.has_attached_file(name, options = {})
        super(name, options)

        send(:"before_#{name}_validate") do
          attachment = send(name)
          check_image_dimension(attachment)
          set_file_content_type(attachment)
          obfuscate_file_name(attachment)
          set_file_extension(attachment)
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1359: a model that declares an attachment without touching the media-type option is not reported"
  lang ruby
  file app/models/media_attachment.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-043
  code
  ```
  class MediaAttachment < ApplicationRecord
    IMAGE_MIME_TYPES = %w(image/jpeg image/png image/gif).freeze

    has_attached_file :file,
                      styles: ->(f) { file_styles f },
                      processors: ->(f) { file_processors f },
                      convert_options: { all: '-quality 90 +profile "!icc,*" +set modify-date +set create-date' }

    validates_attachment_content_type :file, content_type: IMAGE_MIME_TYPES
    validates_attachment_size :file, less_than: IMAGE_LIMIT
  end
  ```

test "rank1359: an attachment that keeps media-type validation enabled is not reported"
  lang ruby
  file app/models/import.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-043
  code
  ```
  class Import < ApplicationRecord
    has_attached_file :data, validate_media_type: true

    validates_attachment_content_type :data, content_type: ['text/csv', 'text/plain']
  end
  ```
